<title>USA: TABLE -American Communications sells notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE -American Communications sells notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from American Communications Services Inc was priced Friday via lead manager BT Securities Corp, according to a market source.</p>
<p>The offering was increased to $220 million from an original size of $170 million, the source added.</p>
<p>American Communications Services is a local exchange carrrier that offers voice and data services to customers in mid-sized markets in the southern U.S.</p>
<p>BORROWER AMERICAN COMMUNICATIONS SERVICES INC</p>
<p>AMT $220 MLN	 COUPON 13.75 PCT  MATURITY 7/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S N/R   YIELD 13.75 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P N/R	 SPREAD +755 BPS   CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTES: The notes include a 2.5 year pre-funded interest</p>
<p>reserve; three-equity call for 35 percent of the issue at</p>
<p>113.75.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
